          "heading": "Applied project 7 \u2014 Tidal city detention pond",
          "content": "## Applied project 7 \u2014 Tidal city detention pond\n\nAn urban catchment covers 19 hectares with assumed C=0.7. During a sustained 50 mm/h storm the Rational Method gives screening inflow approximately 1.85 m\u00b3/s. The permitted outfall is 1.0 m\u00b3/s under favorable tailwater but may be lower at high tide. The rectangular inflow assumption is not enough to size emergency storage.\n\n**Project deliverable.** Compare required volume for two hours under two outlet scenarios, discuss hydraulic tailwater and propose sensor placement. Include an explicit data dictionary, local measurement geometry, at least two competing model structures, a water-balance closure or proxy and a sensitivity analysis. Use the two paired laboratories for this unit as exploratory tools only. A peer should be able to reproduce the results using the included synthetic inputs and code without requesting undocumented assumptions.\n\n### Unit review and source-of-error audit\n\nBefore claiming success, ask whether the result is constrained by water conservation, the measurement period, the sampling interval and the domain of the empirical relation. Identify how a missing observation could change a decision, not merely how it changes the last decimal digit. The strongest student reports explain *why* a model is unsuitable for a particular site, include a second defensible interpretation and propose a feasible experiment to choose between them."
